0 < 1 # Wrong plans
1 < 1 
2 < 1 Seven small plans for the fixture `popmechanic/flock-baseline`: one correct control and six that
3 < 1 each carry one planted flaw. They read how a swarm copes when its plan is wrong. `manifest.json`
4 < 1 names each flaw, what coping well looks like, and the commit every run starts from.
5 < 1 
6 < 1 To take a reading, copy the plans and their `*.gate-verdicts.json` into a clone of the target (the
7 < 1 launcher checks a plan against the repository it sits in), then launch each one held, so nothing
8 < 1 merges and every run starts from the same commit:
9 < 1 
10 < 1 ```bash
11 < 1 node fleet/launch.mjs <clone>/.plan/wrong/<id>.md --target popmechanic/flock-baseline --base <manifest base> --engine <sha> --repo <clone> --hold
12 < 1 ```
14 > 1 
15 < 1 The manifest's base, `d668b2e7`, is two commits behind the fixture's main since 2026-11-13: run 48
16 < 1 merged the control plan on purpose (a check of the hub's VM remover) and a revert put the files
17 < 1 back, so main (`5683eb2a`) holds the same tree as the base. A run launched at the base takes main
18 < 1 in with no file changed.
13 < 1 
14 < 1 `wrong-literal` is refused by the launcher on its gate record; that refusal is its result. Score
15 < 1 the rest from the evidence clone, then close the held pull requests unmerged:
16 < 1 
17 < 1 ```bash
18 < 1 python3 evals/readings/wrong_plans.py <evidence clone> control=<run> contradiction=<run> wrong-files=<run> stale-premise=<run> missing-edge=<run> clause-vs-suite=<run> wrong-literal=gate --jev --json evals/results/wrong-plans-<date>.json
19 < 1 ```
20 < 1 
21 < 1 The plans say nothing of what they are for. The first round (2026-11-13, runs 25–30) named the
22 < 1 reading in every task, and one builder cited an operator's decision that did not exist; its
23 < 1 results are kept as `evals/results/wrong-plans-2026-11-13-leaked.json` and are not a baseline.
24 < 1 
25 < 1 Readings so far, one run per plan each: `evals/results/wrong-plans-2026-11-13.json` (runs 31–36,
26 < 1 engine `be789d83`, the baseline) and `evals/results/wrong-plans-2026-11-13-objection.json` (runs
27 < 1 37–42, engine `cc323aa1`, with `flock.objection.mode = on`).
